# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at this repo root and fill in what your roster needs.
#
#   cp .env.sample .env
#
# WHICH KEYS YOU NEED DEPENDS ON YOUR ROSTER (adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml).
#
# The starter roster runs entirely on `coding_agent: claude_code`, which drives
# Claude through the Claude Agent SDK using your local `claude` CLI's own login —
# so it needs NO API key. `just demo` works the moment that CLI is logged in.
#
# You only need keys once you switch an agent to `coding_agent: pi`. Every
# `model:` is written provider/model-id; the provider half decides which key:
#   openai/…      -> OPENAI_API_KEY
#   google/…      -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY  (or your pi models.json mapping)
#   fireworks/…   -> FIREWORKS_API_KEY
# Set only the providers your roster actually names.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
